<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princess Wencheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 680</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princess Wencheng was a member of the Tang imperial clan who was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> in 641 as a bride for the royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songtsen-gampo">Songtsen Gampo</a>, sealing peace with the emperor Taizong after a Tibetan attack on the Tang frontier. Tibetan tradition credits her with bringing the Jowo statue of the Buddha now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jokhang">Jokhang</a>, and she became a lasting symbol of Sino-Tibetan relations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/princess-wencheng.jpg" alt="Princess Wencheng" width="276" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst Stavro Blofeld · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Princess_Wencheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
